# Normalise line endings.
#
# Everything is stored LF in the repo and checked out as-is. Without this, commits
# made on Windows store CRLF, and the macOS and Linux CI runners then check out files
# whose endings differ from what a contributor on those platforms would produce —
# which shows up as whole-file diffs that hide the real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: the shell requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they fail to execute on macOS and Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.syso binary

# Keep GitHub's language bar honest. The vendored gateway client is upstream code
# carrying local patches, not ours, and lockfiles are generated — counting either as
# authored Go/JS misrepresents what this project actually is.
third_party/** linguist-vendored
frontend/package-lock.json linguist-generated
go.sum linguist-generated

# Collapse lockfile noise in pull request reviews.
frontend/package-lock.json -diff
go.sum -diff
